  "details": "My idea is being able to set a public avatar that's quest ready as a default model that quest users see. \nSo just find an avatar that's quest capable, select an option \"set as quest default\" or something and then change into any other avatar you want and if its not quest compatible then it will use your default as the avatar quest users see instead of the default \"PC User\" avatar. It would be a lot easier on average users not willing to or not knowing how to make a quest ready avatar and prevent quest players from seeing this. \n(Post linked not by me all credit reserved for OP) https://www.reddit.com/r/VRchat/comments/bx8n6v/meme_vrchat_on_oculus_quest_be_like/",
